      "question": "What helps protect skin and eyes from ultraviolet rays?",
      "sample": 0,
      "warmup": false,
      "kind": "GENERATED",
      "text": "[essentials-f1c425461e39b7df] Sun protection is necessary to protect your skin and eyes against harsh UV rays that are responsible for sunburns and skin cancer.",
      "raw_draft": "[S1] Sun protection is necessary to protect your skin and eyes against harsh UV rays that are responsible for sunburns and skin cancer.",
      "prompt": "Dated source excerpts. Differences may reflect scope or conditions, not a resolved contradiction.\n[S1] NPS Ten Essentials\nDate: 2026-05-28 page updated; retrieved 2026-09-30\nSource: https:\/\/www.nps.gov\/articles\/10essentials.htm\nSUN PROTECTION – Sunglasses, sunscreen, and hat Sun protection is necessary to protect your skin and eyes against harsh UV rays that are responsible for sunburns and skin cancer. Consider using sunglasses, sunscreen, and hats. Sun-protection clothing such as pants and long sleeve shirts can also help minimize your exposure to the sun.\n\n[S2] NPS Ten Essentials\nDate: 2026-05-28 page updated; retrieved 2026-09-30\nSource: https:\/\/www.nps.gov\/articles\/10essentials.htm\nILLUMINATION – Flashlight and headlamp Lighting is important in the outdoors at night, and can help you find your way out or signal for help. Items include flashlights, and headlamps. Headlamps are the recommended light source because they are hands-free. Be sure to pack extra batteries.\n\nQuestion: What helps protect skin and eyes from ultraviolet rays?\nUse one or two lines, adding a second only for supported detail.\nStart each line with source labels and then one factual sentence. Answer:",
