        {
          "id": "essentials-f1c425461e39b7df",
          "text": "SUN PROTECTION – Sunglasses, sunscreen, and hat Sun protection is necessary to protect your skin and eyes against harsh UV rays that are responsible for sunburns and skin cancer. Consider using sunglasses, sunscreen, and hats. Sun-protection clothing such as pants and long sleeve shirts can also help minimize your exposure to the sun.",
          "url": "https:\/\/www.nps.gov\/articles\/10essentials.htm",
          "rights": "National Park Service; ten-category system credited to The Mountaineers, Mountaineering: The Freedom of the Hills, 8th edition (2010); NPS explanatory text only; Public domain in the United States; https:\/\/www.nps.gov\/aboutus\/disclaimer.htm"
        },
        {
          "id": "essentials-e772a5a729be28b9",
          "text": "ILLUMINATION – Flashlight and headlamp Lighting is important in the outdoors at night, and can help you find your way out or signal for help. Items include flashlights, and headlamps. Headlamps are the recommended light source because they are hands-free. Be sure to pack extra batteries.",
